      "citation_count": 37,
      "cited_by_count": 37,
      "is_oa": true,
      "oa_status": "gold",
      "abstract": "In this paper, we mainly study the Gardner equation that models the propagation of dust ion acoustic waves. By using the Exp-function method, abundant traveling wave solutions like bright solitary, bright-dark solitary, dark solitary (type-1, type-2, type-3, type-4) and periodic wave solutions or compact-like solutions (type-1, type-2, type-3, type-4) are constructed. The behaviors of the solutions are illustrated through the 3-D contours and 2-D curves. The obtained results show that the proposed method is straightforward, powerful and can provide more forms of the traveling wave solutions, which are expected to be helpful for the study of the traveling wave theory in dusty plasmas.",
